      "text": "Manuel Antonio National Park"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "599b938d0fd7403f285bd59aad9a5fd2e5d85762066e29253f8da53cde39962c",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw8vshb5-enc7ju",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Today you'll explore Manuel Antonio National Park, home to monkeys, sloths, many species of birds, reptiles and butterflies.\n\nA scenic walk of about 2 miles takes you through the tropical forest to a beach that Forbes named among the most beautiful in the world. The forest opens onto white sand and the blue waters of the Pacific Ocean. There is a 20-minute stop at the beach.\n\nYour guide will help you spot local plants and wildlife along the way, so keep your camera handy.\n\nOvernight at Hotel San Bada.\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast."
    },
    {
